 "about_text": "Weinstein Gallery was founded in San Francisco in 1992 by Rowland Weinstein, with a focus on non-objective and surrealist art spanning pre-war Europe through the New York School and Abstract Expressionism. The gallery represents the estates of Rudolf Bauer and Juanita Guccione, and is known for championing women of the surrealist movement, including Leonor Fini, Leonora Carrington, Kay Sage, Stella Snead, Remedios Varo and Dorothea Tanning. It has also worked to revive attention to understudied artists such as Enrico Donati, Jimmy Ernst, Gordon Onslow Ford, Gerome Kamrowski and Kurt Seligmann through exhibitions, publications and museum loans. In Spring 2026 the gallery plans to open a project space in Los Angeles devoted to contemporary art, performance and multidisciplinary programming, extending its historical program into a dialogue with the present day.",
 "source_kind": "official",
